  "serving": {
    "source": "serving",
    "notes": "vLLM validates the k-pool tail requirement, allocates a sparse top-k buffer with tail room rounded to 128 columns, stores compressed indexer states at one state per index_kpool tokens, keeps a raw tail cache for incomplete pools, fuses KDA projections/kernels, and fuses deferred mHC post/pre across adjacent layers. MTP serving can reuse top-k between draft iterations; base decoder layers do not reuse top-k for this checkpoint because every indexer_types entry is full."
